Certificate data
----------------
  upstream-data/S8_n5372.txt
    An eight-coloring of 1..5372 with no monochromatic x + y = z (x = y
    allowed), i.e. a witness for S(8) >= 5372. Taken verbatim from the
    arXiv ancillary files of:

      Zhiyang Chen, Ligeng Zhu, Fan Long,
      "A new lower bound for the sixth Schur number: S(6) >= 537",
      arXiv:2610.31362  https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31362

    Author repository: https://github.com/jeffchen006/Schur-Number-6
    SHA-256 of S8_n5372.txt as published in the authors' SHA256SUMS:
      d0abd71d8de5749bcd12c6bbbb909033a3f8baa17a624364751669b6cb586d24
    (verified on download; see upstream-data/SHA256SUMS for the full table).

    Per the authors, this coloring is obtained from their S(6) >= 537
    partition (certificate.col, also in upstream-data/) via the width-10
    template of Bengone et al.; their check.py re-derives and checks it.

  upstream-data/certificate.col and upstream-data/check.py are likewise the
  authors' ancillary files, redistributed here so the provenance chain is
  self-contained.

